// Chapter 3 — the temple. Door routes converge on an arrival check, then the altar.

=== temple.door
@title The Sealed Door

{image("temple-door", "Moss-covered stairs lead to a sealed stone door carved with a spiral, a closed eye and a hand.")}

A door of a single slab blocks the top of the stair. Three glyphs are cut deep into it: a spiral, a closed
eye, a hand.

* [Trace the glyphs and press the hand] (requires: flag:knows-glyphs) { faction:explorers-guild += 5; player:xp += 50 } -> temple.hall
* [Force the door] skill-check athletics dc 14
  success: { set flag:door-damaged; faction:explorers-guild -= 10 } -> temple.hall
  failure: { player:hp -= 2 } -> temple.side
* [Look for another way in] -> temple.side

=== temple.side
Around the side of the temple, roots have pried open a gap between the stones. It's tight, dark and smells
of something old.

* [Squeeze through] { player:xp += 10 } -> temple.hall
* [Back to the temple door] -> temple.door

=== temple.hall
@title The Hall of Eyes

~ player:xp += 25

Light from your {item:torch} slides over walls carved with thousands of eyes, all closed{if flag:door-damaged}, and
over the cracks your forcing left in the doorway{/if}.

::: skill-check perception dc 13
success: -> temple.niche
failure: -> temple.altar
:::

=== temple.niche
One of the eyes is open. Behind it, in a niche no bigger than your fist, sits a small {item:idol}.

* [Take the idol] { give player idol; player:xp += 50 } -> temple.altar
* [Leave it be] -> temple.altar

=== temple.altar
@title The Altar

{image("relic-altar", "A pale gold disc rests on a worn stone altar beneath walls carved with closed eyes.")}

At the heart of the temple, on an altar worn smooth by centuries of nothing, lies the **{item:relic}**:
a disc of pale gold, warm as skin.

> guide: {player:first-name}. Whatever you do next, the guild will hear about it.

* [Take the relic] { give player relic; player:xp += 100 } -> ending.return
* [Leave it where it lies] -> ending.return
